Add a patch-generation capability to discver so that each PoV-backed confirmed crash also gets a validated fix. Follow the AIxCC de-facto pipeline: root-cause analysis -> generate -> validate -> emit. Requirements:

SCOPE: Only operate on CONFIRMED, PoV-backed crashes (the reproduced ones with a PoV on disk — these are the ones with a real test oracle). Never attempt patches for unverified LLM leads or static-only findings; they have no oracle to validate against.

NEW MODULE src/patch_generator.py, invoked in the final-analysis phase after crash confirmation/dedup, behind a flag (env DISCVER_GENERATE_PATCHES, default OFF so nothing changes unless enabled). Per confirmed crash:
1. ROOT CAUSE: assemble context for the LLM — the crash trace/ASAN output, the crashing function AND its surrounding code (imports, types, helpers it depends on — not just the crashing line; missing context is the #1 cause of non-compiling patches), the sink location, and the taint/data-flow path if available. Ask the model for a root-cause analysis first, then a minimal fix that addresses the ROOT CAUSE across all affected locations (may be multi-hunk / multi-file), not a band-aid at the crash site.
2. GENERATE: produce the fix as concrete edited file(s). Keep it minimal — smallest change that fixes the root cause while preserving intended behavior.
3. VALIDATE IN-CONTAINER (this is the gate — a patch is only emitted if it PASSES): apply the patch to a copy of the source, REBUILD the target in the container, then require BOTH: (a) re-running the PoV no longer triggers the crash/sanitizer, AND (b) the project's existing tests/build still pass (no regressions). If build fails or either check fails, feed the exact error back to the model and retry, bounded (e.g. max 3 attempts). Never emit an unvalidated patch.
4. EMIT (only on pass): write to output/patches/<crash-id>/ the FULL patched file(s) alongside the ORIGINAL file(s) for side-by-side manual review, plus a short PATCH_NOTES.md stating: the vulnerability, root cause, what changed and why, and the validation result (PoV neutralized + tests pass). Do NOT auto-apply to the source tree — human applies manually.

RECORD: for each confirmed crash, log whether a validated patch was produced, failed after retries, or was skipped — via the discver.reliability logger and the run report, so we can measure patch success rate.

SAFETY: never emit a patch that wasn't validated; never touch the confirmed-crash/PoV detection path; default-off flag. Add tests (patch-context assembly, the pass/fail gate logic with a stubbed builder, retry-on-failure, emit-only-on-pass). Verify with py_compile and tests. Update CHANGELOG/README Agent Status. Report the design and how validation hooks into the container build. Commit.
